  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 758890,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## Nord and Bert Couldn't Make Head or Tail of It - Commodore 64\n\nStep into a world turned topsy-turvy in *Nord and Bert Couldn't Make Head or Tail of It*, a delightfully quirky interactive fiction adventure for the Commodore 64! Developed by Infocom and released in 1987, this unique game throws aside traditional logic puzzles in favor of clever wordplay and surreal humor.\n\nAs the player, you find yourself in the town of Punster, where idioms and clichés have sprung to life, creating bizarre and hilarious situations. The game is structured as a series of independent \"short stories,\" each dedicated to a different style of wordplay, from grocery store homonyms to literal interpretations of farm clichés and 1950s sitcom gags. \n\nSolve puzzles by typing in the correct words and phrases, often requiring a playful manipulation of language.  \"The Shopping Bizarre\" might require you to identify \"chocolate mousse\" for a hoofed, antlered mammal, while \"Buy the Farm\" demands you embrace phrases like \"beat swords into plowshares.\"  Unlock the final chapter, \"Meet the Mayor,\" by mastering the previous seven, and prepare for a truly unforgettable, and wonderfully absurd,"
    },
